{"title":"Undefined","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Undefined is used for values that cannot be defined, or have no meaning. Undefined \"values\" occur when an expression is evaluated for input values outside of its domain. This is most commonly represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e36d49dcc915824465fbd749228d6d26a8c23d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Undefined&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082705\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.005 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.008 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 182/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.459      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.459      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18734:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082705 and revision id 240358. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}